 ## Overview
-This method computes the forward projection of a volume defined by box splines and its analytical gradients with respect to ray parameters (origin $t$ and direction $n$) and volume data coefficients [S1, unofficial]. It solves the problem of differentiable X-ray transform (XRT) for uniform grids, supporting 2D and 3D domains with interpolation orders 0, 1, and 2 [S1, unofficial]. Unlike standard differentiable renderers that rely on finite differences or implicit automatic differentiation through the entire ray-marching loop, this method explicitly computes ray-traced geometry gradients using specific adjoint functions for ray anchors and directions, while using the standard adjoint transform for volume coefficients [S1, unofficial]. It is primarily used in geometry calibration for tomography [S1, unofficial].
